\begin{note}
A \emph{decorator} is a function that takes a function and returns a function.
The syntax \lstinline{@decorate def f(x): ...}
is ``syntactic sugar'' for \lstinline{f = decorate(f)}.
Decorators are the reason you can attach behavior (like memoization)
to a recursive function in one line
instead of rebinding the name every time.
\end{note}
